  <compounddef id="group__channel__setters" kind="group">
    <compoundname>channel_setters</compoundname>
    <title>Setters</title>
    <sectiondef kind="func">
      <memberdef kind="function" id="group__channel__setters_1ga5d2369a88f8570d5b6e913cc2e161fdc" prot="public" static="no" const="no" explicit="no" inline="no" virt="non-virtual">
        <type>const int</type>
        <definition>const int ndxlSetChannelParams</definition>
        <argsstring>(NDXLChannel *_Channel, void *_Params)</argsstring>
        <name>ndxlSetChannelParams</name>
        <param>
          <type><ref refid="ndxlcore_8h_1a40b73c1a687ab1376515b42d4294c079" kindref="member">NDXLChannel</ref> *</type>
          <declname>_Channel</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>void *</type>
          <declname>_Params</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Sets the user-defined <computeroutput>void* _Params</computeroutput> of a noise channel. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">_Channel</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Target channel to update the parameters of.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">_Params</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Pointer to extra memory used by the channel. May be NULL.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>If _Channel is NULL, returns <ref refid="group__ndxl__err_1gae9261a8e1c9a6cebdc947ee5798cca1e" kindref="member">NDXL_ERR</ref>, otherwise updates the parameters of _Channel, and returns NDXL_OK.</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="warning"><para>NDXL stores the supplied <computeroutput>void* _Params</computeroutput> pointer without copying the associated data or managing its lifetime. The pointed-to memory must remain valid for as long as the channel uses it.</para>
</simplesect>
This function replaces the channel&apos;s existing parameter pointer without freeing or otherwise managing the memory it previously referenced. The user remains responsible for managing both the previous and new allocations.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="par"><title>Errors raised</title><para><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para><ref refid="group__ndxl__err_1gaf6b8bdcb87bdd7944810152b510101e4" kindref="member">NDXL_ARG_ERR</ref> : _Channel is NULL.</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="see"><para><ref refid="group__channel__getters_1gad111628d528bc1c1955f392cef292423" kindref="member">ndxlGetChannelParams</ref> </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
